  <h2>The Problem</h2>
  <p>
    Municipal tap water meets legal safety standards that were written decades before PFAS,
    microplastics, and pharmaceutical residues were detected in water supplies. The legal
    threshold and the biological safety threshold are not the same number. Fluoride directly
    suppresses thyroid function at chronic exposure levels. Chlorine and chloramine byproducts
    (trihalomethanes) are documented carcinogens. PFAS "forever chemicals" disrupt hormone
    signaling and accumulate in tissue.
  </p>
  <p>
    Shower and bath exposure adds a second route: chlorinated hot water creates inhalation
    exposure to volatile byproducts and skin absorption that can exceed oral ingestion in
    total daily load. Most men who filter their drinking water have never addressed shower
    exposure.
  </p>
  <p>
    Water filtration is one of the most straightforward, one-time interventions available
    in the 4M environmental protocol. The cost-per-day of a quality filtration system
    is lower than almost any supplement in the stack — and it eliminates a daily source of
    biological interference that supplements cannot compensate for.
  </p>

  <h2>The Insulting Behaviors</h2>
  <ul class="insult-list">
    <li>Drinking unfiltered tap water daily — fluoride, PFAS, chlorine, chloramines, and microplastics with every glass</li>
    <li>Using plastic water bottles — microplastics and endocrine-disrupting compounds leach into the water, especially with heat</li>
    <li>Showering in unfiltered hot water — chlorine volatilizes and is inhaled and absorbed through skin</li>
    <li>Filtering drinking water only — ignoring bathing, cooking, and ice as additional exposure routes</li>
    <li>Never replacing filter cartridges — an expired filter delivers contaminants plus whatever has grown in the filter media</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="section-eliminate">Eliminate the Insulting Behavior</h2>
  <div class="card-grid">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Step 1 — Under-Sink Reverse Osmosis</h3>
      <p>RO removes fluoride, PFAS, heavy metals, nitrates, chlorine, and microplastics at the point of use. The most comprehensive drinking-water intervention available.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Step 2 — Shower Filter</h3>
      <p>A KDF or vitamin C shower filter removes chlorine and chloramine from shower water. Protects the skin microbiome and eliminates inhalation exposure during hot showers.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Step 3 — Switch to Glass or Stainless Steel</h3>
      <p>Eliminate all plastic food and water containers — especially single-use plastic bottles left in cars or exposed to heat. This is free.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Step 4 — Whole-Home Filtration (Upgrade Path)</h3>
      <p>A whole-home carbon filter protects all water entry points — drinking, cooking, bathing, and laundry. The most comprehensive option for high-exposure or well-water households.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

